VALUES
  ('PKG-028', 'Kovačica Naïve Art Ateliers & Banat Craft Heritage', 'Ateljei naivnog slikarstva u Kovačici i zanatsko nasleđe Banata', 'History', 'Explore the vibrant ateliers of Slovak Naïve art masters in Kovačica, observe authentic easel craftsmanship, and discover Banat''s traditional textile weaving and ceramic heritage.', 'Istražite živopisne ateljee slovačkih majstora naivne umetnosti u Kovačici, posmatrajte autentičnu izradu i otkrijte tradicionalno tekstilno tkanje i keramičko nasleđe Banata.', 'Kovačica is a global phenomenon where the local Slovak minority has fostered a unique school of Naïve Art since the 1940s. Beyond the Gallery of Naïve Art, this deep experience takes visitors into active home studios of master painters like Zuzana Halupova''s legacy atelier, local violin crafting workshops, and traditional Banat looms. Paired with slow Pannonian gastronomy at local ethno-farms, this day celebrates authentic ethnic art preservation and Pannonian cultural intimacy.', 'Kovačica je svetski fenomen u kome je lokalna slovačka manjina od 1940-ih negovala jedinstvenu školu naivne umetnosti. Pored Galerije naivne umetnosti, ovo iskustvo vodi posetioce u aktivne kućne ateljee majstora slikarstva, radionice za izradu violina i tradicionalne banatske razboje. Uz sporu panonsku gastronomiju na lokalnim etno-farmama, ovaj dan slavi autentično očuvanje etničke umetnosti.', '/src/assets/images/kovacica_naive_art_gallery_1778844026577.webp', 'Full Day', '1 hour', 60, 'Kovačica & Padina, Banat', 'Kovačica i Padina, Banat', '€50–€100', 'Car', 45.1118, 20.8039, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('149', 'Museum of Contemporary Art Belgrade', 'Muzej savremene umetnosti Beograd', 'History', 'Belgrade''s premiere venue for 20th and 21st-century Yugoslav and Serbian modern art, housed in a celebrated 1965 modernist landmark in Ušće Park.', 'Vodeći beogradski muzej jugoslovenske i srpske moderne i savremene umetnosti 20. i 21. veka, smešten u čuvenom modernističkom zdanju u parku Ušće.', 'Designed by Ivanka Raspopović and Ivan Antić and opened in 1965, the Museum of Contemporary Art in Belgrade (MSUB) is an architectural masterpiece of Yugoslav modernism. Situated at the confluence of the Sava and Danube rivers in Ušće Park, the museum features six interconnected crystalline cubes bathed in natural overhead light. Its collection of over 8,000 works captures the vibrant avant-garde, surrealist, and conceptual movements of Yugoslav art from 1900 to the present day.', 'Muzej savremene umetnosti u Beogradu (MSUB), otvoren 1965. godine po projektu Ivanke Raspopović i Ivana Antića, predstavlja remek-delo jugoslovenske modernističke arhitekture. Smešten na ušću Save u Dunav u parku Ušće, muzej se odlikuje sa šest kristalnih kubusa ispunjenih prirodnim svetlom. Njegova bogata zbirka od preko 8.000 dela prikazuje avangardne, nadrealističke i konceptualne umetničke pokrete od 1900. godine do danas.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Museum_of_Contemporary_Art_in_Belgrade.jpg/1280px-Museum_of_Contemporary_Art_in_Belgrade.jpg', '2 - 3 hours', '15 - 20 minutes', 20, 'Ušće Park, Belgrade', 'Park Ušće, Beograd', '€5 - €10', 'Walk / Bus / Taxi', 44.8194, 20.4422, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('150', 'Princess Ljubica’s Residence', 'Konak kneginje Ljubice', 'History', 'An authentic 19th-century royal residence blending Ottoman Balkan architectural roots with Central European interior influences, located in historic Kosančićev Venac.', 'Autentični vlastelinski konak iz 19. veka koji spaja balkansko-osmansko graditeljstvo sa srednjoevropskim enterijerskim uticajima u istorijskom Kosančićevom vencu.', 'Built between 1829 and 1831 under Prince Miloš Obrenović for his family and Princess Ljubica, this historic palace stands as a crucial transitional monument in Belgrade''s architectural history. Located in Kosančićev Venac near the St. Michael''s Cathedral, the residence combines traditional Balkan-Ottoman architectural elements—such as a central divanhana and bay windows—with European Classicist interior decoration. Today operating under the City Museum of Belgrade, it houses authentic 19th-century furniture, Biedermeier salons, and historic portrait collections.', 'Sagrađen između 1829. i 1831. godine po nalogu kneza Miloša Obrenovića za njegovu porodicu i kneginju Ljubicu, ovaj istorijski dvorac predstavlja ključni spomenik arhitektonske tranzicije u Beogradu. Smešten na Kosančićevom vencu u blizini Saborne crkve, konak spaja balkansko-orijentalne elemente poput divanhane i doksata sa evropskim klasicističkim enterijerom. Danas u sastavu Muzeja grada Beograda, čuva autentični nameštaj iz 19. veka, bidermajer salone i zbirku portreta.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Konak_kneginje_Ljubice_01.jpg/1280px-Konak_kneginje_Ljubice_01.jpg', '1 - 1.5 hours', 'Urban walk', 10, 'Kosančićev Venac, Belgrade', 'Kosančićev venac, Beograd', '€3 - €6', 'On Foot', 44.8173, 20.4519, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('151', 'Nebojša Tower', 'Kula Nebojša', 'History', 'A monumental 15th-century artillery tower at the foot of Belgrade Fortress, guarding the Danube rivergate with multimedia exhibitions on Balkan freedom struggles.', 'Monumentalna artiljerijska kula iz 15. veka u podnožju Beogradske tvrđave koja je čuvala dunavsko pristanište, danas multimedijalni izložbeni prostor.', 'Constructed around 1460 by the Hungarians during the reign of King Matthias Corvinus, Nebojša Tower is the best-preserved medieval cannon tower of the Belgrade Fortress lower town. Standing at the water gate of the Sava and Danube rivers, this octagonal four-story stone bastion played a critical role in defending the city against Ottoman besiegers. In later centuries, the Ottomans converted the tower into a notorious dungeon where Greek revolutionary hero Rigas Feraios was imprisoned and executed in 1798. Today, a modern multimedia exhibition spans four floors, chronicling Danube defense history, Ottoman imprisonment, and the 19th-century Balkan struggles for independence.', 'Sagrađena oko 1460. godine za vreme ugarskog kralja Matije Korvina, Kula Nebojša predstavlja najbolje očuvanu srednjovekovnu topovsku kulu Donjeg grada Beogradske tvrđave. Ova osmougaona kamena kula na vodenoj kapiji imala je ključnu ulogu u odbrani grada od Osmalija. Kasnije je pretvorena u tamnicu u kojoj je 1798. poginuo grčki revolucionar Rigas od Fere. Danas se u njoj nalazi savremena multimedijalna postavka na četiri nivoa posvećena istoriji rečne odbrane, osmanskom tamnovanju i borbi balkanskih naroda za oslobođenje.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Kula_Nebojsa_Beograd.jpg/1280px-Kula_Nebojsa_Beograd.jpg', '1 - 1.5 hours', 'Urban walk', 10, 'Lower Town, Belgrade Fortress', 'Donji grad, Beogradska tvrđava', '€3 - €5', 'On Foot', 44.8267, 20.4481, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('152', 'Gallery of Matica Srpska', 'Galerija Matice srpske', 'History', 'The cultural treasure chest of Novi Sad, presenting three centuries of Serbian fine art from post-Byzantine icons to 20th-century modernism.', 'Kulturna riznica Novog Sada sa preko tri veka srpske likovne umetnosti, od postvizantijskih ikona do modernizma 20. veka.', 'Founded in Budapest in 1847 and relocated to Novi Sad in 1864, Matica Srpska is the oldest cultural and scientific institution of the Serbian people. Its art gallery, housed in an elegant Neoclassical building on Trg Galerija, holds over 10,000 works representing national visual culture from the 18th to the 20th century. Highlights include rare post-Byzantine icon painting, 19th-century Biedermeier and Romantic masterworks by Uroš Predić and Paja Jovanović, and early modernism. The gallery is celebrated for its accessible curation, tactile stations, and rich educational programming.', 'Osnovana u Pešti 1847. godine i preseljena u Novi Sad 1864, Matica srpska je najstarija kulturna i naučna institucija srpskog naroda. Njena galerija na Trgu galerija čuva preko 10.000 umetničkih dela od 18. do 20. veka. Među najznačajnijim eksponatima su ikone iz postvizantijskog perioda, remek-dela romantizma i realizma Uroša Predića i Paje Jovanovića, kao i dela ranog modernizma. Galerija je poznata po savremenom pristupu izlaganju, dodirnim stanicama i inovativnim programima.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Galerija_Matice_srpske_2019.jpg/1280px-Galerija_Matice_srpske_2019.jpg', '1.5 - 2.5 hours', '1 hour (from Belgrade)', 60, 'Trg Galerija, Novi Sad', 'Trg galerija, Novi Sad', '€3 - €6', 'Soko Train / Car', 45.2533, 19.845, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('153', 'Bajrakli Mosque', 'Bajrakli džamija', 'History', 'Belgrade''s sole surviving Ottoman mosque, built around 1575 in historic Dorćol, preserving authentic stone Islamic architecture.', 'Jedina sačuvana beogradska osmanska džamija iz 1575. godine na Dorćolu, spomenik islamske arhitekture u Srbiji.', 'Constructed around 1575 during Ottoman rule, the Bajrakli Mosque is the only active historic mosque remaining out of more than 200 that once stood in Belgrade. Situated in the historic Dorćol neighborhood on Gospodar Jevremova street, the single-domed stone structure features a stone minaret and classic Ottoman architectural proportions. Historically known as the ''Flag Mosque'' because the signal flag for prayer was raised here to prompt other city mosques, it remains an active place of worship and a powerful testament to Belgrade''s multi-religious heritage.', 'Sagrađena oko 1575. godine tokom osmanske vladavine, Bajrakli džamija je jedina sačuvana od nekadašnjih preko 200 beogradskih džamija. Smeštena u Jevremovoj ulici na Dorćolu, ova jednokupolna kamena građevina sa minaretom nosi naziv ''Bajrakli'' (sa barjakom) jer se na njoj isticao barjak kao znak za početak molitve u ostalim džamijama. Danas je aktivni verski objekat i značajan spomenik multikonfesionalnog nasleđa Beograda.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Bajrakli_dzamija_Beograd_1.jpg/1280px-Bajrakli_dzamija_Beograd_1.jpg', '30 - 45 minutes', 'Urban walk', 10, 'Dorćol, Belgrade', 'Gospodar Jevremova, Dorćol, Beograd', 'Free / Donation', 'On Foot', 44.8219, 20.4578, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('154', 'Archaeological Hall of National Museum Niš', 'Arheološka sala Narodnog muzeja Niš', 'History', 'A concise archaeological treasure house in Niš, housing extraordinary Roman imperial artifacts from Naissus and Mediana.', 'Bogata arheološka postavka Narodnog muzeja u Nišu sa dragocenim rimskim i antičkim nalazima iz Naisa i Medijane.', 'Located on Stanka Paunovića street in central Niš, the Archaeological Hall of the National Museum Niš displays the region''s rich archaeological record from the Neolithic to the Middle Ages. The collection''s core centerpiece comprises world-class Roman imperial artifacts discovered at ancient Naissus and the Mediana imperial villa—including marble statues of Asclepius and Hygieia, Roman bronze military helmets, gold jewelry, and Constantine-era coins and inscriptions. It provides an indispensable intellectual foundation before or after visiting the nearby Mediana archaeological site.', 'Smeštena u centru Niša u ulici Generala Milojka Lešjanina, Arheološka sala Narodnog muzeja Niš prikazuje bogato arheološko nasleđe ovog kraja od neolita do srednjeg veka. Okosnicu postavke čine neprocenjivi antički nalazi iz antičkog Naisa i carske vile Medijane—uključujući mermerne skulpture Asklepija i Higije, rimske bronzane šlemove, zlatan nakit i kovanice iz doba cara Konstantina. Poseta sali predstavlja savršenu uvodnu celinu pre obilaska same Medijane i Niške tvrđave.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Narodni_muzej_Nis_01.jpg/1280px-Narodni_muzej_Nis_01.jpg', '1 - 1.5 hours', '2.5 hours (from Belgrade)', 150, 'Central Niš', 'Centar Niša', '€2 - €4', 'Car / Bus / Train', 43.3211, 21.8961, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('155', 'Majkin Salaš (Palić / Subotica)', 'Majkin Salaš (Palić)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A quintessential North Bačka farmstead estate offering slow-cooked Vojvodina specialties, homemade rakija, traditional tamburica music, and sprawling orchards near Lake Palić.', 'Karakteristično severnobačko salašarsko imanje sa tradicionalnim kuvanim jelima, domaćom rakijom i tamburašima.', 'Spread over several hectares of lush orchards and farmland near Palić, Majkin Salaš preserves the authentic lifestyle of traditional Bačka farmsteads. Built with natural materials, adobe, and wooden beams, the estate serves legendary regional dishes—gulaš cooked in clay pots, riblja čorba, home-baked bread, and poppy-seed štrudla—accompanied by local fruit spirits and live tamburica music.', 'Prostrano vojvođansko imanje pored Palića sa starinskim kućama od čerpića i drveta, voćnjacima i restoranom u kome se poslužuju gulaš iz zemljanih lonaca, pečenje, domaća štrudla sa makom i voćne rakije uz zvuk tamburice.', '/src/assets/images/salas_ethno_farm_food_1778847386244.webp', '3 - 4 hours', '2 hours (from Belgrade) / 10 mins (from Subotica)', 120, 'Palić / Subotica', 'Palić', '€20 - €40', 'Car / Bus', 46.0682, 19.7425, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('156', 'Perkov Salaš (Neradin, Fruška Gora)', 'Perkov Salaš (Neradin)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'An intimate family ethno-household tucked in the southern foothills of Fruška Gora, renowned for heirloom recipes, homemade jams, and warm Srem hospitality.', 'Autentično sremsko etno-domaćinstvo u podnožju Fruške gore sa starinskim jelima i domaćim pekmezima.', 'Nestled in the village of Neradin on Fruška Gora, Perkov Salaš is an authentic Srem ethno-farmstead surrounded by vineyards and plum orchards. Managed by the Šević family, the estate preserves century-old tools, traditional woven textiles, and open-hearth kitchens where slow-cooked Srem stew, domestic bread, and famous sausages are served alongside elderberry juice and Bermet wine.', 'Porodični salaš u Neradinu okružen vinogradima i šljivicima. Domaćini poslužuju domaći hleb, sremski gulaš, sušeno meso i bermet u ambijentu prepunom muzejskih starina i sremske tradicije.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Fruska_Gora_Landscape.jpg/1280px-Fruska_Gora_Landscape.jpg', '3 - 4 hours', '1 hour (from Belgrade) / 30 mins (from Novi Sad)', 60, 'Neradin, Fruška Gora', 'Neradin', '€20 - €35', 'Car / Minibus', 45.1189, 19.8911, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('157', 'Sunčana Reka Ethno Complex (Drina River)', 'Sunčana Reka (Drina)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A riverside ethno-haven on the banks of the emerald Drina River, offering fresh river trout, roasted lamb under the bell, and traditional Podrinje hospitality.', 'Etno-naselje na samoj obali reke Drine sa rečnom pastrmkom, pečenjem ispod sača i prostranim drvenim terasama.', 'Set directly on the bank of the Drina River between Banja Koviljača and Gučevo Mountain, Sunčana Reka is a sprawling ethno-resort crafted from natural stone, wood, and brick. Guests enjoy authentic Podrinje cuisine—fresh Drina river trout, slow-roasted lamb under the bell (sač), domestic proja, and kajmak—served on outdoor wooden terraces overlooking the river.', 'Jedinstven kompleks na obali smaragdne Drine ispod planine Gučevo. Restoran nudi drinsku pastrmku, teletinu i jagnjetinu pod sačem, vruću proju i kajmak u opuštajućem rečnom okruženju.', '/src/assets/images/drina_soft_rafting_river_1778848188991.webp', '3 - 4 hours', '2 hours (from Belgrade)', 120, 'Banja Koviljača / Drina River', 'Banja Koviljača', '€25 - €45', 'Car / Tour Bus', 44.5298, 19.1672, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('158', 'Moravski Konaci (Velika Plana)', 'Moravski Konaci (Velika Plana)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A restored 19th-century Morava wooden village set around an artificial lake in Central Serbia, serving Šumadija roasts, wedding cabbage, and local wines.', 'Rekonstruisano srpsko selo iz 19. veka oko jezerceta sa pečenjem, svadbarskim kupusom i lepinjama.', 'Situated near Velika Plana along the Great Morava river valley, Moravski Konaci is a reconstructed 19th-century Serbian village featuring authentic wooden chalets, a wooden church, a watermill, and a central lake. The lakeside restaurant serves traditional Šumadija dishes including roast pork, svadbarski kupus in earthenware pots, teleća čorba, and fresh domaća pogača with kajmak.', 'Etno-selo u Pomoravlju sa brvnarama, vodenicom i jezerom. Restoran poslužuje tradicionalni svadbarski kupus iz grnčarije, teleću čorbu, pečenje i vruću pogaču sa kajmakom.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Velika_Plana_Landscape.jpg/1280px-Velika_Plana_Landscape.jpg', '3 - 4 hours', '1 hour (from Belgrade)', 60, 'Velika Plana', 'Velika Plana', '€20 - €40', 'Car / Highway', 44.3312, 21.0822, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('159', 'Salaš Katai (Mali Iđoš)', 'Salaš Katai (Mali Iđoš)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A vibrant multicultural ethno-farm in the heart of Bačka, offering Hungarian and Serbian country feast traditions, bakeries, and horse-drawn wagons.', 'Multikulturalni bački salaš sa mađarskim i srpskim specijalitetima, starinskom pekarom i vožnjom zapregom.', 'Located in Mali Iđoš, Salaš Katai is a unique farmstead experience celebrating the joint Serbian and Hungarian culinary heritage of central Vojvodina. The farm includes a traditional bakery with clay wood-fired ovens, domestic animal paddocks, and a rustic dining hall serving goulash, pörkölt, homemade fruit jams, freshly baked pogátsa, and fruit brandies made from estate-grown plums and apricots.', 'Jedinstveno seosko imanje u Malom Iđošu koje spaja kulinarsku tradiciju Srba i Mađara. Domaćinstvo obuhvata pekaru sa paorskim pećima, domaće životinje i restoran gde se poslužuju perkelt, gulaš, pogačice i voćne rakije.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Mali_Idjos_Landscape.jpg/1280px-Mali_Idjos_Landscape.jpg', '3 - 4 hours', '1.5 hours (from Belgrade) / 45 mins (from Novi Sad)', 90, 'Mali Iđoš', 'Mali Iđoš', '€20 - €35', 'Car / Highway', 45.7061, 19.6631, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('160', 'Etno Selo Srna (Stara Planina)', 'Etno Selo Srna (Stara Planina)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A tranquil mountain ethno-refuge at the foot of Stara Planina, celebrating East Serbian highland gastronomy, Pirot cheeses, and forest herbs.', 'Planinsko etno-imanje u podnožju Stare planine sa belmužom, pirotskim kačkavaljem i pečenjem pod sačem.', 'Nestled in the pristine village of Inovo near Knjaževac at the base of Stara Planina, Etno Selo Srna is built from natural mountain stone and timber. The tavern serves rare East Serbian culinary treasures—stara planina lamb under the bell, peglana kobasica (ironed sausage), staroplaninski sir (hard mountain cheese), belmuž (traditional cheese-corn dish), and wild berry liquors—amidst crisp mountain air and babbling trout streams.', 'Kameno-drveni kompleks u selu Inovo pored Knjaževca. Restoran priprema autentične istočnosrpske specijalitete: belmuž, peglanu kobasicu, staroplaninski kačkavalj i jagnjetinu pod sačem uz šum gorskih potoka.', '/src/assets/images/stara_planina_landscape_1778843454764.webp', '3 - 4 hours', '3.5 hours (from Belgrade) / 1.5 hours (from Niš)', 210, 'Inovo, Knjaževac / Stara Planina', 'Knjaževac / Stara Planina', '€20 - €40', 'Car', 43.4617, 22.4283, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('161', 'Babina Reka Ethno Estate (Lazarevac)', 'Babina Reka (Lazarevac)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A serene oasis surrounded by streams, stone bridges, and oak woods on the edge of Šumadija, offering slow-cooked country banquets and artistic relaxation.', 'Šumadijsko etno-imanje okruženo potocima i hrastovom šumom sa domaćim gibanicama i pečenjem.', 'Situated in the peaceful countryside near Lazarevac (~60 km south of Belgrade), Babina Reka ("Grandmother''s River") is a secluded ethno-estate featuring stone houses, rustic wooden bridges, ponds, and sculpture gardens created by local artists. The farm restaurant offers slow-cooked Šumadija delicacies—roasted pork, homemade cheese pies, sour milk, grilled trout, and quince brandy—in a picturesque woodland setting.', 'Skrivena oaza u selu Trbušnica kod Lazarevca sa kamenim kućicama, mostićima i ribnjakom. Restoran priprema pečenje, domaću gibanicu, kiselo mleko i dunjevaču u idiličnom prirodnom okruženju.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Lazarevac_Landscape.jpg/1280px-Lazarevac_Landscape.jpg', '3 - 4 hours', '1 hour (from Belgrade)', 60, 'Trbušnica, Lazarevac', 'Lazarevac', '€20 - €40', 'Car', 44.3389, 20.3528, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('162', 'Vrdnička Kula Ethno Village (Fruška Gora)', 'Etno Selo Vrdnička Kula (Vrdnik)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A refined hilltop ethno-resort nestled in dense pine woods beneath medieval Vrdnik Tower, offering premium Srem cuisine and estate wines.', 'Precalculiran etno-restoran u borovoj šumi ispod Vrdničke kule sa sremskim pečenjem, divljači i bermetom.', 'Located inside Fruška Gora National Park just below the historic medieval Vrdnik Tower, Ethno Village Vrdnička Kula combines traditional Srem architecture with upscale country comfort. Built from wood and stone, its panoramic restaurant serves gourmet interpretations of Srem and Vojvodina classics—slow-cooked wild game stew, roasted pork shoulder, domestic cheeses, and regional Bermet wines.', 'Ekskluzivno etno-naselje u sklopu Nacionalnog parka Fruška gora. Restoran od drveta i kamena nudi gurmanski srneći gulaš, sporopečeno pečenje, domaće sireve i vrhunska sremska vina.', '/src/assets/images/fruska_gora_monastery_vineyard_1778842911981.webp', '3 - 4 hours', '1 hour (from Belgrade) / 25 mins (from Novi Sad)', 60, 'Vrdnik, Fruška Gora', 'Vrdnik', '€25 - €50', 'Car', 45.1322, 19.7891, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('163', 'Zornića Kuća (Baćevac, Barajevo)', 'Zornića Kuća (Baćevac)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'An eco-friendly Šumadija ethno-household just 35km from Belgrade, featuring a wood-fired bakery, organic farm-to-table roasts, and panoramic rolling hills.', 'Nagrađivano šumadijsko etno-domaćinstvo na 35km od Beograda sa pečenjem pod sačem, konjima i orgaskom hranom.', 'Located in Baćevac near Barajevo, Zornića Kuća is an award-winning rural estate blending authentic Šumadija timber architecture with modern organic farming principles. The estate features an open-air wood oven, riding stables, an ethno museum, and an outdoor restaurant serving homemade proja, kajmak, veal under the bell, duvan čvarci, and domestic rakija with stunning views of the Šumadija hills.', 'Poznato seosko imanje u Baćevcu sa drvenim kućama, konjušnicom i pećima na drva. Restoran nudi teletinu pod sačem, duvan čvarce, proju sa kajmakom i prirodne voćne sokove sa pogledom na šumadijske brežuljke.', '/src/assets/images/salas_ethno_farm_food_1778847386244.webp', '3 - 4 hours', '40 mins (from Belgrade)', 40, 'Baćevac, Barajevo', 'Baćevac / Barajevo', '€20 - €45', 'Car / Taxi', 44.5781, 20.3752, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('164', 'Gostoljublje Rural Household (Mionica / Maljen)', 'Gostoljublje (Mionica / Maljen)', 'Gastronomy, Travel', 'A traditional Western Serbia farmstead in the foothills of Mount Maljen, famous for clay-pot kačamak, domestic kajmak, plum orchards, and genuine mountain village hospitality.', 'Seosko domaćinstvo u podnožju Maljena sa domaćim kajmakom, kačamakom, vajatima i šljivicima.', 'Situated in Mionica village near Kosjerić and Mount Maljen, Gostoljublje ("Hospitality") is a pristine rural household run by the Vujić family. Guests gather in traditional wooden vajats surrounded by plum orchards and pastures to enjoy organic mountain breakfasts—freshly churned kajmak, hot gibanica, kačamak with sour milk, roasted lamb under the bell, and homemade šljivovica brandy.', 'Autentično seosko imanje porodice Vujić u Mionici podno Maljena. U tradicionalnim vajatima i voćnjacima poslužuju se planinski kačamak, vruća gibanica, jagnjetina pod sačem i domaća šljivovica.', '/src/assets/images/divcibare_pine_forest_1778845837560.webp', '3 - 4 hours', '2 hours (from Belgrade)', 120, 'Mionica / Kosjerić, Maljen', 'Mionica / Kosjerić', '€20 - €35', 'Car', 44.0219, 19.9234, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-006', 'Pirot Kilim Weaving & Stara Planina Wilderness', 'Pirotsko ćilimarstvo i divljina Stare planine', 'Travel, Heritage', 'Discover centuries-old UNESCO-candidate Pirot kilim hand-weaving traditions in the shadow of Stara Planina’s dramatic alpine peaks, waterfalls, and traditional stone villages.', 'Otkrijte viševekovnu tradiciju ručnog tkanja pirotskog ćilima u podnožju dramatičnih vrhova, vodopada i kamenih sela Stare planine.', 'Pirot is Serbia’s capital of carpet-weaving, famous for flat-woven kilims created on vertical looms using dense local sheep wool and natural dye recipes guarded for centuries. The geometric patterns and spiritual symbols reflect Balkan and Ottoman influences. Towering above the city, Stara Planina (Balkan Mountains) offers wild alpine pastures, red rock gorges, and pristine waterfalls. Exploring Pirot’s weaving ateliers alongside Stara Planina’s mountain villages presents an authentic encounter with ancient mountain culture and living folk art.', 'Pirot je prestonica srpskog ćilimarstva, čuvena po ćilimima tkanim na vertikalnom razboju od lokalne vune i prirodnih boja. Geometrijske šare i ornamentika nose duboko simbolicno značenje. Iznad grada izdiže se Stara planina sa divljim pašnjacima, klisurama i vodopadima. Obilazak tkačkih radionica uz planinska sela pruža autentičan susret sa starim planinskim nasleđem.', '/src/assets/images/pirot_kilim_weaving_craft_1778847353764.webp', 'Full day to weekend', '3.5 - 4 hours', 220, 'Pirot & Stara Planina', 'Pirot i Stara planina', 'Moderate', 'Car', 43.1531, 22.5861, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-007', 'Felix Romuliana & Negotin Stone Wine Cellars', 'Feliks Romulijana i Rajačke pimnice', 'History, Travel', 'Immerse in late Roman imperial grandeur at UNESCO-listed Felix Romuliana, paired with authentic wine tasting in the ancient stone pimnice cellars of Rajačke & Rogljevačke Pimnice.', 'Zakoračite u poznorimski carski sjaj UNESKO lokaliteta Feliks Romulijana, uz degustaciju vina u drevnim kamenim pimnicama Negotinske krajine.', 'Felix Romuliana (Gamzigrad) is a magnificent Late Roman imperial palace built by Emperor Galerius in the late 3rd and early 4th centuries, featuring monumental defensive towers, intricate floor mosaics, and temples. A short drive east leads to the Negotin Valley, celebrated for its unique stone wine villages (''pimnice'') in Rajac and Rogljevo. These 18th- and 19th-century stone cellars, built exclusively for wine making and aging, preserve indigenous grape varieties like Prokupac and Tamjanika. Together, they form an extraordinary journey linking Roman imperial heritage with Eastern Serbia’s viticultural culture.', 'Feliks Romulijana (Gamzigrad) je velepni poznorimski carski dvorac cara Galerija sa monumentalnim kulama, mozaicima i hramovima. U blizini, u Negotinskoj krajini, nalaze se Rajačke i Rogljevačke pimnice — kamena sela građena isključivo za proizvodnju i čuvanje vina. Spoj carskog nasleđa i vinarske tradicije čini ovaj region jedinstvenim na Balkanu.', '/src/assets/images/felix_romuliana_ruins_1778841314415.webp', '1 - 2 Days', '3 hours', 180, 'Zaječar & Negotin Valley', 'Zaječar i Negotinska krajina', 'Moderate', 'Car', 43.8992, 22.1856, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-008', 'Tara Mountain Sanctuary & Drina Canyon', 'Nacionalni park Tara i kanjon Drine', 'Nature, Travel', 'Surround yourself with ancient pine forests, panoramic clifftop lookouts over the emerald Drina River, and endemic Omorika spruce trees in West Serbia’s wild heart.', 'Uživajte u drevnim borovim šumama, vidikovcima iznad smaragdne Drine i Pančićevoj omorici u srcu zapadne Srbije.', 'Tara National Park is West Serbia’s pristine mountain sanctuary, renowned for dense pine and beech forests, dramatic karst limestone canyons, and the rare Pančić spruce (Omorika)—a living fossil tree species. Lookouts such as Banjska Stena present breathtaking vertical panoramas over the turquoise meanders of the Drina River Canyon. Visitors can indulge in serene forest walks, e-biking, kayaked river views, and rustic mountain gastronomy in a serene, eco-rich atmosphere.', 'Nacionalni park Tara je netaknuto planinsko utočište poznato po gustim šumama, kanjonima i Pančićevoj omorici. Vidikovci poput Banjske stene pružaju veličanstven pogled na meandre reke Drine. Idealan izbor za planinarenje, biciklizam i uživanje u prirodi.', '/src/assets/images/tara_national_park_forest_1778843961956.webp', '1 - 3 Days', '3.5 hours', 210, 'Tara National Park & Bajina Bašta', 'Nacionalni park Tara', 'Moderate', 'Car', 43.9111, 19.4681, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-016', 'Niš Imperial Heritage & Monumental Memory', 'Carsko nasleđe Niša i spomenici istorije', 'History, Travel', 'Journey from the birthplace of Emperor Constantine at the Mediana villa complex through the Ottoman Stambol Gate to the poignant Skull Tower (Ćele Kula).', 'Prošetajte od rodnog mesta cara Konstantina na Medijani, preko osmanske Tvrđave, do jedinstvenog spomenika Ćele-kula.', 'Niš stands at the crossroads of Balkan history. Mediana, the luxury summer residence of Emperor Constantine the Great, showcases more than 1,000 m² of preserved Roman mosaics and thermal baths. Across the Nišava River, the 18th-century Ottoman Niš Fortress guards the city center with its Stambol Gate and hammam. The journey culminates at Ćele Kula (Skull Tower), a uniquely historic 1809 monument built by Ottoman forces following the Battle of Čegar. Together with authentic Southern Serbian gastronomy in Kazandžijsko Sokače alley, this experience links classical antiquity, Ottoman heritage, and national memory.', 'Niš je vekovna raskrsnica Balkana. Rimska vila Medijana otkriva više od 1.000 m² očuvanih mozaika i termalnih kupatila. Tvrđava iz 18. veka čuva gradsko jezgro, dok Ćele-kula svedoči o oslobodilačkim borbama iz 1809. godine. Uz autentičnu južnjačku gastronomiju u Kazandžijskom sokačetu, ovo je jedno od najbogatijih istorijskih putovanja u Srbiji.', '/src/assets/images/mediana_roman_villa_1778845820866.webp', 'Full Day', '2.5 hours', 150, 'Niš & Mediana', 'Niš i Medijana', 'Moderate', 'Car', 43.3209, 21.8958, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-017', 'Đavolja Varoš & Prolom Mineral Sanctuary', 'Đavolja Varoš i Prolom Banja', 'Nature, Wellbeing', 'Discover around 200 remarkable earth pillars capped with stone blocks at Devil''s Town, paired with thermal mineral relaxation in Prolom Spa.', 'Istražite oko 200 zemljanih figura sa kamenim kapama u Đavoljoj Varoši uz relaksaciju u visokoalkalnim vodama Prolom Banje.', 'Nestled in the Radan Mountains of South Serbia, Đavolja Varoš (Devil''s Town) is a rare natural monument featuring around 200 remarkable earth pillars topped with protective stone caps. Formed by centuries of acidic water erosion and mineral weathering, the towers stand beside red acidic mineral springs. Nearby, Prolom Banja provides a high-alkaline thermal mineral retreat surrounded by untouched oak forests. This experience pairs intriguing geomorphological wonders with therapeutic wellness.', 'Smeštena na planini Radan, Đavolja Varoš predstavlja prirodni fenomen sa oko 200 jedinstvenih zemljanih kupa sa kamenim blokovima na vrhu. Nastale viševekovnom erozijom, ove figure stoje pored crvenih kiselih izvora. U neposrednoj blizini, Prolom Banja nudi oporavak u visokoalkalnoj mineralnoj vodi okruženoj gustim šumama.', '/src/assets/images/davolja_varos_pillars_1778841249456.webp', 'Full Day', '3.5 hours', 210, 'Kuršumlija & Radan Mountain', 'Kuršumlija i planina Radan', 'Moderate', 'Car', 42.9933, 21.4036, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-018', 'Resava Underground Palace & Lisine Karst Cascade', 'Resavska pećina i vodopad Lisine', 'Nature, Travel', 'Descend into Resava Cave''s 80-million-year-old subterranean halls before dining beside the roaring Veliki Buk waterfall in Lisine.', 'Spustite se u dvorane Resavske pećine stare 80 miliona godina, a zatim uživajte pored huka vodopada Veliki Buk u Lisinama.', 'Resava Cave is one of Serbia''s oldest and most magnificent speleological treasures, carved over 80 million years with multi-colored stalactites, stalagmites, and stone draperies. Nearby, the Beljanica mountain slopes give rise to Lisine (Veliki Buk), a spectacular karst waterfall cascading over tufa deposits into a crystal-clear pool. Shaded trout restaurants along the river serve freshly caught fish and traditional homestead specialties, creating a peaceful excursion into Pomoravlje''s subterranean and karst wonders.', 'Resavska pećina je jedan od najstarijih i najlepših speleoloških objekata u Srbiji, sa bogatim pećinskim nakitom u crvenim, žutim i belim nijansama. U podnožju Beljanice nalazi se vodopad Lisine (Veliki Buk), gde se bistra voda obrušava preko tufa. Restorani pored reke nude svežu kalifornijsku pastrmku i domaće specijalitete pomoravskog kraja.', '/src/assets/images/resava_cave_formations_1778845766990.webp', 'Full Day', '1.5 hours', 90, 'Despotovac & Beljanica', 'Despotovac i Beljanica', 'Moderate', 'Car', 44.0933, 21.6289, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('PKG-024', 'Vrnjačka Banja Mineral Springs & Thermal Wellness', 'Vrnjačka Banja i termalni wellness', 'Wellbeing, Travel', 'Stroll through Austria-Hungary-style promenade gardens, cross the historic Bridge of Love, and enjoy mineral springs and thermal wellness in Serbia’s royal spa town.', 'Prošetajte parkovima u stilu austrougarskih banja, obiđite čuveni Most ljubavi i opustite se u prirodnim lekovitim izvorima.', 'Celebrated since Roman antiquity as Aquae Orcinae and patronized by 19th-century Serbian royalty, Vrnjačka Banja is Serbia’s premier thermal sanctuary. The promenade weaves past classic fin-de-siècle villas, shaded parks, and seven distinct mineral springs. Local tradition associates the Bridge of Love (Most ljubavi) with one of the earliest love-lock stories dating to the First World War. Paired with fresh mountain trout dining along the Goč foothill streams and high-end hydrotherapy at local spa sanctuaries, this day offers total mental and physical rejuvenation.', 'Poznata još od rimskog doba kao Aquae Orcinae i pod pokroviteljstvom srpskih dinastija, Vrnjačka Banja je kraljica srpskog turizma. Šetalište spaja secesijske vile, senovite parkove i sedam mineralnih izvora. Lokalna tradicija povezuje Most ljubavi sa pričom iz Prvog svetskog rata. Uz gastronomski užitak sveže pastrmke sa podnožja Goča i savremene wellness tretmane, ovo putovanje nudi potpunu obnovu energije.', '/src/assets/images/vrnjacka_banja_1778841098566.webp', 'Full Day', '2.5 hours', 150, 'Vrnjačka Banja & Goč', 'Vrnjačka Banja i Goč', 'Moderate', 'Car', 43.6261, 20.8928, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('103', 'The Wild Karst of Eastern Serbia (Lazarev Canyon + Zlot Caves)', 'Divlji krš Istočne Srbije (Lazarev kanjon + Zlotske pećine)', 'Nature', 'Explore Lazarev Canyon, the deepest and longest canyon in eastern Serbia, coupled with the magnificent caverns of Zlot. A rugged, dramatic karst ecosystem featuring spectacular natural viewpoints, rich biodiversity, and deep prehistoric cave passages.', 'Explore Lazarev Canyon, the deepest and longest canyon in eastern Serbia, coupled with the magnificent caverns of Zlot. A rugged, dramatic karst ecosystem featuring spectacular natural viewpoints, rich biodiversity, and deep prehistoric cave passages.', 'Lazarev Canyon is a dramatic limestone gorge carved into the eastern foothills of the Kučaj mountains. As the deepest canyon in eastern Serbia, its vertical limestone cliffs harbor unique tertiary flora and fauna. Coupled with the Zlot Caves—specifically Lazareva Pećina, famous for its ancient homonid remains, fossilized cave bear bones, and pristine stalactite galleries—this experience presents an adventurous escape into the untamed karst heartland of the country.', 'Lazarev Canyon is a dramatic limestone gorge carved into the eastern foothills of the Kučaj mountains. As the deepest canyon in eastern Serbia, its vertical limestone cliffs harbor unique tertiary flora and fauna. Coupled with the Zlot Caves—specifically Lazareva Pećina, famous for its ancient homonid remains, fossilized cave bear bones, and pristine stalactite galleries—this experience presents an adventurous escape into the untamed karst heartland of the country.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', 'Full day', '3 - 3.5 hours', 210, 'Near Bor', 'Near Bor', '€15 - €30', 'Car', 44.032, 21.961, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('109', 'Between Two Mountains (Ovčar-Kablar Active Day)', 'Između dve planine (Ovčarsko-kablarska klisura)', 'Nature', 'An immersive outdoor day in the ''Serbian Mount Athos'' gorge. Combines hiking through dramatic river bends with visits to monasteries hidden in dense forest.', 'An immersive outdoor day in the ''Serbian Mount Athos'' gorge. Combines hiking through dramatic river bends with visits to monasteries hidden in dense forest.', 'The Ovčar-Kablar Gorge is carved by the West Morava River, separating the peaks of Ovčar and Kablar mountains. Renowned for its ten medieval monasteries built into the cliffs during Ottoman times, the region offers a harmonious blend of pristine nature and deep religious heritage. This active route takes travelers along winding paths, offering fresh mountain air, mineral spring wells, and historic stone architecture.', 'The Ovčar-Kablar Gorge is carved by the West Morava River, separating the peaks of Ovčar and Kablar mountains. Renowned for its ten medieval monasteries built into the cliffs during Ottoman times, the region offers a harmonious blend of pristine nature and deep religious heritage. This active route takes travelers along winding paths, offering fresh mountain air, mineral spring wells, and historic stone architecture.', '/src/assets/images/ovcar_kablar_gorge_monastery_1778844065335.webp', 'Full day', '2 hours', 120, 'Near Čačak', 'Near Čačak', '€10 - €30', 'Car + Hike', 43.903, 20.187, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('113', 'A Morning Among the Birds (Carska Bara)', 'Jutro među pticama (Carska bara)', 'Nature', 'A spectacular wetland reserve in Vojvodina hosting hundreds of rare migratory bird species. Enjoy quiet boat rides and photography among fields of water lilies.', 'A spectacular wetland reserve in Vojvodina hosting hundreds of rare migratory bird species. Enjoy quiet boat rides and photography among fields of water lilies.', 'Carska Bara (The Imperial Pond) is an exceptional marshland ecosystem situated near the Begej River. Home to over 250 species of birds, including rare herons and cormorants, it is an international Ramsar wetland. Boat cruises navigate the quiet waterways under dense willow galleries, offering travelers a peaceful morning of birdwatching, soft light photography, and absolute silence.', 'Carska Bara (The Imperial Pond) is an exceptional marshland ecosystem situated near the Begej River. Home to over 250 species of birds, including rare herons and cormorants, it is an international Ramsar wetland. Boat cruises navigate the quiet waterways under dense willow galleries, offering travelers a peaceful morning of birdwatching, soft light photography, and absolute silence.', '/src/assets/images/carska_bara_wetlands_birds_aerial_1778846483752.webp', 'Half day', '1 hour', 60, 'Near Zrenjanin', 'Near Zrenjanin', '€5 - €15', 'Car + Boat', 45.253, 20.395, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('116', 'Tara’s Manuscript Trail (Rača Monastery + Surrounding Landscape)', 'Rukopisni tragovi Tare (Manastir Rača)', 'Nature', 'A gentle walking trail in Tara National Park linking the historical Rača Monastery to clear mountain springs. Blends dense woodlands with medieval monastic literacy lore.', 'A gentle walking trail in Tara National Park linking the historical Rača Monastery to clear mountain springs. Blends dense woodlands with medieval monastic literacy lore.', 'This tranquil route begins at Rača Monastery, founded in the 13th century and famous for preserving the Serbian Cyrillic script during Ottoman rule. The path follows the crystal-clear Rača River through thick beech and spruce forests to the emerald-green ''Ladjevac'' thermal spring, representing a peaceful pilgrimage of heritage and nature.', 'This tranquil route begins at Rača Monastery, founded in the 13th century and famous for preserving the Serbian Cyrillic script during Ottoman rule. The path follows the crystal-clear Rača River through thick beech and spruce forests to the emerald-green ''Ladjevac'' thermal spring, representing a peaceful pilgrimage of heritage and nature.', '/src/assets/images/manasija_monastery_1778841065960.webp', '3-4 hours', '3.5 hours', 210, 'Tara National Park', 'Tara National Park', 'Free', 'Car + Walk', 43.931, 19.542, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('117', 'Eastern Serbia Discovery Weekend', 'Vikend otkrivanja Istočne Srbije', 'Nature', 'A curated multi-stop nature circuit winding through eastern Serbia''s dense forests, limestone cliffs, and rushing water springs.', 'A curated multi-stop nature circuit winding through eastern Serbia''s dense forests, limestone cliffs, and rushing water springs.', 'Designed as a comprehensive road trip, this route connects the most spectacular natural landmarks of Eastern Serbia, including Krupaj Spring, Ždrelo Gorge, and the majestic waterfalls of Veliki Buk. Travelers discover a region steeped in ancient Vlach traditions, rich geological architecture, and rustic mountain taverns serving local Homolje honey and sheep''s cheese.', 'Designed as a comprehensive road trip, this route connects the most spectacular natural landmarks of Eastern Serbia, including Krupaj Spring, Ždrelo Gorge, and the majestic waterfalls of Veliki Buk. Travelers discover a region steeped in ancient Vlach traditions, rich geological architecture, and rustic mountain taverns serving local Homolje honey and sheep''s cheese.', '/src/assets/images/djerdap_gorge_danube_1778842863362.webp', 'Weekend', '3 hours', 180, 'Eastern Serbia', 'Eastern Serbia', '€50 - €120', 'Car', 44.464, 22.152, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('125', 'Royal Serbia in Half a Day (Oplenac + Royal Heritage + Historic Winery)', 'Kraljevska Srbija (Oplenac i Topola)', 'History', 'Visit the spectacular white-marble royal mausoleum of the Karađorđević dynasty in Topola, boasting one of the world''s largest collections of mosaic art.', 'Visit the spectacular white-marble royal mausoleum of the Karađorđević dynasty in Topola, boasting one of the world''s largest collections of mosaic art.', 'Perched atop Oplenac Hill, St. George''s Church houses the tombs of the Serbian and Yugoslav royal family. The interior is decorated with stunning mosaics comprising 40 million tiles in 15,000 different colors, recreating frescoes from Serbia’s finest medieval monasteries. The experience is paired with the historic Royal Winery, founded in 1930 to produce wines on the sun-soaked slopes of Šumadija.', 'Perched atop Oplenac Hill, St. George''s Church houses the tombs of the Serbian and Yugoslav royal family. The interior is decorated with stunning mosaics comprising 40 million tiles in 15,000 different colors, recreating frescoes from Serbia’s finest medieval monasteries. The experience is paired with the historic Royal Winery, founded in 1930 to produce wines on the sun-soaked slopes of Šumadija.', '/src/assets/images/oplenac_mausoleum_mosaics_1778846378714.webp', 'Half day', '1.2 hours', 75, 'Topola', 'Topola', '€15 - €35', 'Car', 44.258, 20.683, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('126', 'Niš Through Its People', 'Niš kroz svoje ljude', 'History', 'A narrative cultural route exploring the layered historical memories of southern Serbia''s largest city, from Roman imperial heritage to dark modern memories.', 'A narrative cultural route exploring the layered historical memories of southern Serbia''s largest city, from Roman imperial heritage to dark modern memories.', 'This curated cultural tour takes travelers through the historical memories of Niš. Highlights include Mediana, the luxury estate of Roman Emperor Constantine the Great; the evocative Skull Tower (Ćele Kula), built by Ottoman forces in 1809; and the historic Niš Fortress, offering a balanced narrative of battlefields, family memory, and southern Serbian hospitality.', 'This curated cultural tour takes travelers through the historical memories of Niš. Highlights include Mediana, the luxury estate of Roman Emperor Constantine the Great; the evocative Skull Tower (Ćele Kula), built by Ottoman forces in 1809; and the historic Niš Fortress, offering a balanced narrative of battlefields, family memory, and southern Serbian hospitality.', '/src/assets/images/nis_fortress_stambol_gate_1778845134540.webp', 'Full day', '2.5 hours', 150, 'Niš', 'Niš', '€15 - €30', 'Car + Walk', 43.321, 21.895, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('129', 'Serbia Before the Crowds', 'Srbija pre gužvi', 'History', 'A carefully curated medieval heritage route guiding you through lesser-known, isolated fortifications and architectural treasures.', 'A carefully curated medieval heritage route guiding you through lesser-known, isolated fortifications and architectural treasures.', 'For travelers seeking quiet authenticity, this route highlights architectural and fortification heritage off the main tourist trail. It includes Soko Grad''s clifftop ruins and Mileševa Monastery—home to the world-famous ''White Angel'' fresco. These isolated valleys offer deep tranquility, uncrowded stone ruins, and honest contact with ancient Serbian history.', 'For travelers seeking quiet authenticity, this route highlights architectural and fortification heritage off the main tourist trail. It includes Soko Grad''s clifftop ruins and Mileševa Monastery—home to the world-famous ''White Angel'' fresco. These isolated valleys offer deep tranquility, uncrowded stone ruins, and honest contact with ancient Serbian history.', '/src/assets/images/gostusa_stone_village_1778846432213.webp', 'Full day', '3.5 hours', 210, 'Central & Southern Serbia', 'Central & Southern Serbia', 'Free', 'Car + Hike', 43.084, 22.842, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('132', 'Wine Among Stone Cellars (Rajačke Pimnice at Dusk)', 'Vino među kamenim pivnicama (Rajačke pimnice u sumrak)', 'Gastronomy', 'A timeless village of 270 hand-carved stone cellars dedicated exclusively to wine. Taste local Prokupac and Tamjanika in medieval atmospheric stone vaults.', 'A timeless village of 270 hand-carved stone cellars dedicated exclusively to wine. Taste local Prokupac and Tamjanika in medieval atmospheric stone vaults.', 'The Rajačke Pimnice (cellars) in eastern Serbia are a unique architectural complex built of local limestone during the 18th and 19th centuries. Erected separate from the human dwellings, these cells are carved into the ground to provide naturally stable temperatures for winemaking. Walking through the narrow dusty paths at dusk feels like stepping into a medieval wine sanctuary, complete with family wine-tasting rooms.', 'The Rajačke Pimnice (cellars) in eastern Serbia are a unique architectural complex built of local limestone during the 18th and 19th centuries. Erected separate from the human dwellings, these cells are carved into the ground to provide naturally stable temperatures for winemaking. Walking through the narrow dusty paths at dusk feels like stepping into a medieval wine sanctuary, complete with family wine-tasting rooms.', '/src/assets/images/rajacke_pimnice_village_1778843436699.webp', 'Half day', '4 hours', 240, 'Rajac Village', 'Rajac Village', '€20 - €50', 'Car', 44.097, 22.548, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('136', 'Native Grapes of Fruška Gora (Small-Producer Wine Journey)', 'Autohtone sorte Fruške gore', 'Gastronomy', 'A curated driving and tasting tour visiting boutique, family-run vineyards specializing in native grapes like Grašac and Sila.', 'A curated driving and tasting tour visiting boutique, family-run vineyards specializing in native grapes like Grašac and Sila.', 'Escape the commercial estates and enter the private tasting tables of Fruška Gora’s boutique wine makers. Discover the renaissance of Grašac (an ancient white variety) and modern blends that benefit from the Danube’s unique micro-climate, paired with home-baked bread, cold cuts, and field view sunset walks.', 'Escape the commercial estates and enter the private tasting tables of Fruška Gora’s boutique wine makers. Discover the renaissance of Grašac (an ancient white variety) and modern blends that benefit from the Danube’s unique micro-climate, paired with home-baked bread, cold cuts, and field view sunset walks.', '/src/assets/images/fruska_gora_ebike_route_1778848222663.webp', 'Half day', '1 hour', 60, 'Fruška Gora Slopes', 'Fruška Gora Slopes', '€25 - €60', 'Car', 45.163, 19.824, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('143', 'Belgrade Through an Architect’s Eyes (Focused Design and Modernism Route)', 'Beograd očima arhitekte', 'Travel', 'A curated walking tour focusing on Belgrade’s design evolution, from Art Nouveau details to brutalist housing blocks and modern galleries.', 'A curated walking tour focusing on Belgrade’s design evolution, from Art Nouveau details to brutalist housing blocks and modern galleries.', 'Step away from standard sightseeing and explore Belgrade’s urban fabric through architectural design blocks. A curated path explores the historic center''s classic Secessionist buildings, the modernist architecture of post-war squares, and active contemporary galleries that trace Serbia''s architectural history.', 'Step away from standard sightseeing and explore Belgrade’s urban fabric through architectural design blocks. A curated path explores the historic center''s classic Secessionist buildings, the modernist architecture of post-war squares, and active contemporary galleries that trace Serbia''s architectural history.', '/src/assets/images/belgrade_design_district_1778845854594.webp', '3 hours', '0.2 hours', 10, 'Belgrade', 'Belgrade', '€10 - €25', 'Walk', 44.818, 20.457, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('144', 'Subotica After Dark', 'Subotica noću', 'History', 'Witness the illuminated Art Nouveau masterpieces of Subotica under soft evening lights, followed by a quiet, refined dinner.', 'Witness the illuminated Art Nouveau masterpieces of Subotica under soft evening lights, followed by a quiet, refined dinner.', 'At sunset, Subotica''s spectacular City Hall, Synagogue, and Secessionist facades are illuminated with warm, architectural spotlights. This creates a peaceful, deeply cinematic design walk, best finished with a glass of native wine and slow dinner in an elegant northern setting.', 'At sunset, Subotica''s spectacular City Hall, Synagogue, and Secessionist facades are illuminated with warm, architectural spotlights. This creates a peaceful, deeply cinematic design walk, best finished with a glass of native wine and slow dinner in an elegant northern setting.', '/src/assets/images/subotica_palic_lake_villa_1778843996440.webp', '3 hours', '2 hours', 120, 'Subotica', 'Subotica', '€20 - €50', 'Car + Walk', 46.1, 19.667, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('147', 'Southern Serbia in Slow Time (Prolom Banja + Carefully Curated Regional Experience)', 'Južna Srbija u laganom ritmu (Prolom Banja)', 'Wellbeing', 'A quiet wellness retreat famous for its highly alkaline Prolom mineral water, coupled with peaceful walks among ancient volcanic cliffs.', 'A quiet wellness retreat famous for its highly alkaline Prolom mineral water, coupled with peaceful walks among ancient volcanic cliffs.', 'Prolom Banja is nestled in southern Serbia, surrounded by the green hills of Radan Mountain. Highly regarded for its pure, mineral-light water, this peaceful spa provides therapeutic programs, forest paths, and scenic stone churches. Paired with a trip to the nearby Devils Town geological pillars, it offers a harmonious, slow-time journey of physical rest and natural exploration.', 'Prolom Banja is nestled in southern Serbia, surrounded by the green hills of Radan Mountain. Highly regarded for its pure, mineral-light water, this peaceful spa provides therapeutic programs, forest paths, and scenic stone churches. Paired with a trip to the nearby Devils Town geological pillars, it offers a harmonious, slow-time journey of physical rest and natural exploration.', '/src/assets/images/prolom_banja_alkaline_spa_1778850911305.webp', 'Weekend', '3.5 hours', 210, 'Southern Serbia', 'Southern Serbia', '€30 - €70', 'Car', 43.042, 21.405, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-01', 'Rtanj Pyramid Summit Ascent', 'Uspon na piramidalni vrh Rtnja', 'Nature', 'Ascend the iconic limestone pyramid peak of Šiljak on Rtanj Mountain, featuring 360-degree views across Eastern Serbia, unique medicinal flora, and legendary local folklore.', 'Slikoviti uspon na piramidalni vrh Šiljak na planini Rtanj sa panoramskim pogledom na istočnu Srbiju i bogatom lekovitom florom.', 'Rtanj Mountain is renowned for its symmetrical pyramidal peak, Šiljak (1,565m). The southern approach trail climbs through dense beech woodland before emerging onto open limestone ridges. Hikers are rewarded with sweeping panoramas of the Timok region, abundant wild herbs such as Rtanj tea (Satureja montana), and the historic ruins of the St. George hilltop chapel.', 'Planina Rtanj je poznata po svom simetričnom piramidalnom vrhu Šiljak (1.565m). Južna staza vodi kroz bukovu šumu i izlazi na otvorene krečnjačke grebene, nudeći veličanstven pogled na timočki kraj.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '5-6 Hours', '2.5 - 3 Hours from Belgrade', 160, 'Boljevac / Rtanj', 'Boljevac / Rtanj', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 43.7761, 21.8903, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-02', 'Midžor High-Peak Summit Ridge', 'Grebenski uspon na Midžor', 'Nature', 'Hike the highest peak of Central Serbia along the serene alpine border ridge of Stara Planina, offering expansive subalpine meadows and open mountain panoramas.', 'Pješačenje na najviši vrh centralne Srbije duž spokojnog visokoplaninskog grebena Stare planine.', 'Midžor (2,169m) forms the summit peak of Stara Planina along the Serbian-Bulgarian border. Departing from the Babin Zub ski refuge area, the trail follows a wide, rolling alpine ridge. The route provides an accessible high-altitude experience free of technical climbing, passing seasonal glacial springs and vibrant alpine grasslands.', 'Midžor (2.169m) predstavlja najviši vrh Stare planine. Staza od Babinog zuba vodi duž prostranog grebena sa kojeg se pružaju otvoreni vidici na alpine livade i okolne planinske lance.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '4-5 Hours', '3.5 - 4 Hours from Belgrade', 220, 'Stara Planina / Knjaževac', 'Stara Planina / Knjaževac', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 43.3958, 22.6806, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-03', 'Suva Planina Ridge Traverse & Trem Peak', 'Grebenska staza Suve Planine i vrh Trem', 'Nature', 'Traverse the dramatic, razor-sharp limestone ridge of Suva Planina to reach Trem Peak (1,810m), experiencing South-Eastern Serbia''s most impressive alpine scenery.', 'Uzbudljiva grebenska staza preko oštrog krečnjačkog masiva Suve Planine do najvišeg vrha Trem (1.810m).', 'Suva Planina ("Dry Mountain") is famed for its horseshoe-shaped karst ridge and vertical limestone cliffs. Starting from Bojanine Vode near Niška Banja, the ascent via Devojački Grob tests stamina before reaching Trem Peak. The trail offers unparalleled exposures and vistas across the Zaplanje valley.', 'Suva Planina je poznata po svojim vertikalnim krečnjačkim stena i potkovičastom grebenu. Uspon od Bojaninih voda preko Devojačkog groba vodi na sam vrh Trem sa koga se pruža pogled na Zaplanje.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '5-6 Hours', '3 Hours from Belgrade', 180, 'Niška Banja / Suva Planina', 'Niška Banja / Suva Planina', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 43.1817, 22.1803, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-04', 'Rajac Alpine Meadow Circuit', 'Kružna staza Rajačkih livada', 'Nature', 'Enjoy accessible high-altitude walking through rolling meadows, conifer groves, and scenic viewpoints on Rajac Mountain, just two hours from Belgrade.', 'Pristupačna planinska šetnja kroz cvetne livade, četinarske šume i vidikovce planine Rajac.', 'Rajac is part of the Suvobor mountain cluster and serves as an approachable haven for gentle hiking. The circular trail connects mountain lodges, memorial monuments from WWI, and grassy ridges overlooking Šumadija. Ideal for day trips, family walking, and traditional mountain dining.', 'Rajac pripada suvoborskom planinskom masivu i nudi pitome staze za šetnju. Kružna staza povezuje planinarske domove, spomenike iz Prvog svetskog rata i prostrane vidikovce nad Šumadijom.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '2-3 Hours', '1.5 - 2 Hours from Belgrade', 100, 'Ljig / Suvobor', 'Ljig / Suvobor', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 44.1378, 20.2181, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-05', 'Veliki Štrbac Danube Gorge Trail', 'Staza Veliki Štrbac nad Đerdapskom klisurom', 'Nature', 'Ascend through Djerdap National Park to Veliki Štrbac peak (768m), taking in towering cliffside views over the narrowest gorge of the Danube River.', 'Uspon kroz Nacionalni park Đerdap do vrha Veliki Štrbac sa koga se pruža pogled na najuži deo Dunava u Kazanu.', 'Overlooking the dramatic Iron Gates (Kazan Gorge), the trail to Veliki Štrbac climbs through dense oak-hornbeam reserves and past the Ploče forest station. At the summit cliffs, hikers look down nearly 800 meters to the swirling turquoise waters of the Danube, where the river narrows to under 150 meters wide.', 'Staza do Velikog Štrpca (768m) vodi kroz šumske rezervate Đerdapa i preko vidikovca Ploče. Sa vršnih stena pruža se nesvakidašnji pogled na Dunav procepljen između uskih krečnjačkih litica.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '4-5 Hours', '2.5 - 3 Hours from Belgrade', 170, 'Djerdap National Park / Donji Milanovac', 'Nacionalni park Đerdap / Donji Milanovac', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 44.6067, 22.2611, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-06', 'Stolovi Wild Horse Ridge Trail', 'Grebenska staza divljih konja na Stolovima', 'Nature', 'Hike the scenic ridge of Stolovi Mountain above the Ibar River valley, where herds of free-roaming horses may be encountered amidst vast, grassy alpine heights.', 'Slikovito pješačenje grebenom planine Stolovi iznad doline Ibra gde se mogu sresti krda slobodnih konja.', 'Stolovi Mountain near Kraljevo is famous for its Kamarište ridge (1,375m) and the semi-wild horse herds that roam freely across its open slopes. Starting from Brezna, the trail wanders across carpeted mountain meadows with views stretching toward Maglič Fortress and the Ibar Gorge.', 'Planina Stolovi pored Kraljeva poznata je po grebenu Kamarište (1.375m) i polu-divljim konjima koji slobodno pasu. Staza iz Brezne vodi preko prostranih livada sa pogledom na dolinu Ibra i tvrđavu Maglič.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '4-5 Hours', '2.5 - 3 Hours from Belgrade', 165, 'Kraljevo / Stolovi Mountain', 'Kraljevo / Planina Stolovi', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 43.6083, 20.6861, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-07', 'Divčibare Twin Peaks Trail', 'Staza dva vrha na Divčibarama', 'Nature', 'A gentle, family-friendly mountain trek on the Maljen plateau, linking the wooded summits and open panoramas of Crni Vrh and Golubac.', 'Prijatna, porodična planinska šetnja platoom Maljena koja povezuje šumovite vrhove Crni Vrh i Golubac.', 'Located in the Valjevo Highlands, Divčibare offers mild mountain walking accessible year-round. This trail connects two prominent peaks—Crni Vrh (1,096m) and Golubac (1,050m)—traversing pine woods, peat meadows, and quiet ridges overlooking Western Serbia.', 'Divčibare na visoravni Maljen nude pristupačne staze tokom cele godine. Ova ruta povezuje Crni Vrh (1.096m) i Golubac (1.050m), vodeći kroz borove šume i mirne vidikovce zapadne Srbije.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '2-3 Hours', '1.5 - 2 Hours from Belgrade', 110, 'Divčibare / Maljen', 'Divčibare / Maljen', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 44.1083, 19.9917, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-08', 'Beljanica Plateau & Waterfall Crest Trail', 'Staza vodopada i visoke platoe Beljanice', 'Nature', 'Experience an active ascent from the lush karst waterfall basin of Lisine up into the solitary, limestone high plateau of Beljanica Mountain (1,339m).', 'Uspon od kraškog vodopada Veliki Buk na Lisine do usamljene krečnjačke visoravni Beljanice (1.339m).', 'Distinct from valley sightseeing, this mountain trail begins at the Veliki Buk karst spring and climbs steadily through beech woodland onto the limestone karst crest of Beljanica. The route opens onto rolling alpine pastures, sinkholes, and sweeping views of Eastern Serbia.', 'Aktivna planinarska staza polazi od vodopada Lisine i kroz bukovu šumu savladava visinu do otvorenog kraškog platoa Beljanice sa vršnim grebenom i kraškim uvalama.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '4-5 Hours', '2 - 2.5 Hours from Belgrade', 140, 'Despotovac / Beljanica', 'Despotovac / Beljanica', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 44.1139, 21.6983, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-09', 'Kopaonik Celestial Ridge & Metođe Walk', 'Kopaoničke Nebeske Stolice i prirodni rezervat Metođe', 'Nature', 'Discover Kopaonik beyond the ski slopes on a high-altitude trail uniting panoramic ridge crests, the ancient Nebeske Stolice sanctuary ruins, and the Metođe nature reserve.', 'Visokoplaninsko pješačenje Kopaonikom van skijališta koje spaja grebenske vidikovce, lokalitet Nebeske Stolice i rezervat Metođe.', 'Away from winter resort infrastructure, Kopaonik National Park reveals pristine subalpine ecosystems. This trail traverses the Nebeske Stolice ("Celestial Chairs") ridge, offering views toward Kosovo and Montenegro, before descending toward the protected sanctuary waters of Metođe spring.', 'Staza vodi preko arheološko-prirodnog lokaliteta Nebeske Stolice na 1.800m nadmorske visine i spušta se ka svetilištu i izvoru Metođe u gustoj smrčevoj šumi.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '3-4 Hours', '3.5 - 4 Hours from Belgrade', 230, 'Kopaonik National Park', 'Nacionalni park Kopaonik', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 43.2858, 20.8256, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('F1-10', 'Povlen Three Peaks Mountain Traverse', 'Traverza tri vrha Povlena', 'Nature', 'Explore the quiet summits of Mali, Srednji, and Veliki Povlen, traversing ancient beech groves and highland pastures in the heart of the Valjevo Mountains.', 'Mirno planinarenje kroz tri vrha Povlena – Mali, Srednji i Veliki Povlen – u srcu Valjevskih planina.', 'Povlen is the highest peak group in the Valjevo mountain range (Mali Povlen 1,347m). The trail links all three main summits, winding through shaded deciduous forests, limestone outcrops, and solitary highland meadows far removed from commercial tourism.', 'Povlen predstavlja najviši masiv Valjevskih planina. Staza spaja Mali, Srednji i Veliki Povlen (1.347m), vodeći kroz bukove šume, krečnjačke stene i osamljene planinske livade.', '/src/assets/images/lazarev_canyon_wild_1778845803839.webp', '4-5 Hours', '2 Hours from Belgrade', 120, 'Valjevo Mountains / Povlen', 'Valjevske planine / Povlen', '€0 - €20', 'Car', 44.1333, 19.7417, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-01', 'Zlakusa Hand-Thrown Pottery Ateliers', 'Ateljei ručno rađene lončarije u Zlakusi', 'History', 'Discover Zlakusa''s ancient hand-thrown clay pottery technique, using a unique blend of clay and calcite ground on stone wheels and wood-fired in open kilns.', 'Otkrijte drevnu tehniku izrade zlakuske lončarije na ručnom kolu, uz korišćenje jedinstvene mešavine gline i kalcita pečene na otvorenoj vatri.', 'Zlakusa pottery represents an unbroken centuries-old ceramic tradition in Western Serbia. Local master potters combine natural clay with coarsely ground calcite mineral on slow manual wheels, shaping vessels before firing them in open wood-fuelled pits. Visitors can observe master artisans shaping traditional bakrač and sač vessels, learn about calcite tempering, and experience authentic rural workshops.', 'Zlakuska lončarija predstavlja vekovnu tradiciju izrade posuđa u zapadnoj Srbiji. Majstori kombinuju prirodnu glinu sa mlevenim kalcitom na ručnom kolu, oblikujući posude koje se peku na otvorenoj vatri. Posetioci mogu posmatrati izradu posuda za sač, upoznati se sa tehnikom kalcitnog vezivanja i obići autentične seoske radionice.', '/src/assets/images/zlakusa_pottery_craft_1778841163739.webp', '1.5–2.5 Hours', '2.5 Hours from Belgrade', 150, 'Zlakusa / Užice', 'Zlakusa / Užice', '€10–€25', 'Car', 43.8053, 19.9881, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-02', 'Pirot Kilim Weaving Looms', 'Tkačke radionice pirotskog ćilima', 'History', 'Observe master weavers crafting world-famous Pirot kilim carpets on vertical looms using two-sided geometric ornamentation and natural wool dyes.', 'Posmatrajte majstorice tkanja kako na vertikalnim razbojima izrađuju čuvene pirotske ćilime sa obostranim geometrijskim šarama i prirodno bojenom vunom.', 'Pirot kilim weaving is an extraordinary cultural heritage art form from South-Eastern Serbia. Hand-woven on vertical looms without reverse sides, each kilim features intricate geometric motifs and symbolic protective iconography passed down through generations. Visits provide intimate insight into wool spinning, natural dyeing processes, and precision loom craftsmanship.', 'Tkanje pirotskog ćilima predstavlja izuzetno kulturno nasleđe jugoistočne Srbije. Izrađeni na vertikalnom razboju bez naličja, ovi ćilimi nose složene geometrijske šare i simbole sa zaštitnim značenjem. Poseta omogućava uvid u pripremu vune, prirodno bojenje i preciznu veštinu tkanja.', '/src/assets/images/pirot_kilim_weaving_craft_1778847353764.webp', '1.5–2 Hours', '3.5 Hours from Belgrade', 210, 'Pirot', 'Pirot', '€10–€30', 'Car', 43.1531, 22.5861, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-03', 'Kovačica Naïve Art Painter Ateliers', 'Ateljei naivnog slikarstva u Kovačici', 'History', 'Immerse yourself in Kovačica''s celebrated Slovak naïve art community, exploring home ateliers filled with vibrant oil canvases depicting rural Banat life.', 'Uronite u poznatu zajednicu slovačkog naivnog slikarstva u Kovačici, obilazeći kućne ateljea ispunjene živopisnim platnima seoskog života u Banatu.', 'Kovačica is Serbia''s celebrated center of self-taught Slovak naïve painting. Since the mid-20th century, local self-taught painters have captured agricultural cycles, folk costumes, village festivals, and Banat landscapes in striking detailed oil compositions. Visitors meet active artists in their home studios, view historical gallery collections, and gain personal appreciation for Banat''s folk art.', 'Kovačica je poznat centar slovačkog samoukog naivnog slikarstva. Od sredine 20. veka, lokalni slikari na platnima objašnjavaju poljoprivredne radove, narodne nošnje i seoske običaje Banata. Posetioci mogu sresti umetnike u njihovim radionicama, obići galerijske zbirke i doživeti autentičnu umetničku viziju seoskog života.', '/src/assets/images/kovacica_naive_art_gallery_1778844026577.webp', '1.5–2.5 Hours', '1 Hour from Belgrade', 60, 'Kovačica / Banat', 'Kovačica / Banat', '€10–€20', 'Car', 45.1111, 20.8039, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-04', 'Sombor Tamburica Lutherie Workshops', 'Graditeljske radionice tambura u Somboru', 'History', 'Explore master lutherie workshops in Sombor where traditional Vojvodina string instruments—from prim to bas-prim—are meticulously crafted by hand.', 'Istražite graditeljske radionice u Somboru gde se tradicionalni žičani instrumenti Vojvodine — od prima do bas-prima — ručno izrađuju od plemenitog drveta.', 'Sombor''s acoustic heritage lives through master luthiers who handcraft traditional tamburica instruments. Selecting aged spruce, maple, and walnut woods, artisans carve soundboards, shape necks, and adjust bridge resonances to achieve the warm, resonant acoustic tone essential to Vojvodina''s musical culture. Visitors gain rare insight into wood seasoning, inlay decoration, and acoustic tuning.', 'Vojvođansko muzičko nasleđe Sombora čuva se kroz radionice graditelja tambura. Odabirom odležanog smrekovog i javorovog drveta, majstori ručno oblikuju korpuse i glasnjače dajući instrumentima specifičan topli ton. Poseta pruža uvid u odabir drveta, finu obradu i zvučnu kalibraciju instrumenata.', '/src/assets/images/sirogojno_knitted_wool_premium_1778847401094.webp', '1.5–2 Hours', '2 Hours from Belgrade', 120, 'Sombor / Bačka', 'Sombor / Bačka', '€10–€25', 'Car', 45.7742, 19.1122, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-05', 'Šumadija Traditional Opanak Leather Craft', 'Opančarske radionice Šumadije', 'History', 'Observe master opančari hand-weaving traditional Serbian leather footwear with distinctive upturned toes (kljun) using vegetable-tanned straps.', 'Posmatrajte opančarske majstore kako ručno pletu tradicionalnu srpsku kožnu obuću sa prepoznatljivim kljunom od prirodno štavljene kože.', 'The opanak is Serbia''s iconic traditional leather footwear, crafted through precise hand-braid techniques. In Šumadija workshops, master leatherworkers strip vegetable-tanned hide into fine ribbons, weaving sole structures and forming the upturned toe horn (kljun) characteristic of Šumadija style. Demonstrations reveal centuries-old tools, leather preparation methods, and historical folk costume traditions.', 'Opanak je simbol srpske narodne nošnje, izrađen preciznim ručnim pletenjem kože. U radionicama Šumadije, opančari seku prirodno štavljenu kožu na trake, pletu gornji deo i oblikuju karakterističan zavijeni kljun. Poseta prikazuje stare alate, pripremu kože i očuvanje tradicionalnog zanata.', '/src/assets/images/sirogojno_ethno_village_1778845118794.webp', '1.5–2 Hours', '1.5 Hours from Belgrade', 90, 'Kragujevac / Šumadija', 'Kragujevac / Šumadija', '€10–€20', 'Car', 44.0128, 20.9114, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-06', 'Gradac & Mionica Active River Watermills', 'Aktivne vodenice na Gradcu i Mionici', 'Nature', 'Visit centuries-old wooden watermills powered by crystal-clear karst rivers, watching heavy millstones turn corn into fresh stone-ground flour.', 'Obiđite vekovne drvene vodenice na čistim kraškim rekama i posmatrajte rad žrvnja koji mlevenjem kukuruza stvara domaće brašno.', 'Along the pristine karst waters of the Gradac River and Kolubara tributaries, historic wooden watermills continue a living milling tradition. Powered by water sluices driving horizontal wheels, heavy natural stones slowly grind local corn, buckwheat, and wheat into nutrient-rich coarse flour. Visitors can watch millers adjust water intake, inspect rustic timber architecture, and purchase freshly ground stone meal.', 'Duž bistrih reka gradačkog kraja i Mionice, stare drvene vodenice i dalje mlevu žito na tradicionalan način. Pokretane rečnim tokom preko drvenog vitla, kamene ploče polako melju kukuruz i pšenicu u integralno brašno. Posetioci mogu posmatrati rad vodenice, uživati u prirodi i kupiti sveže mleveno brašno.', '/src/assets/images/ovcar_kablar_gorge_monastery_1778844065335.webp', '1.5–2.5 Hours', '1.5 Hours from Belgrade', 90, 'Valjevo / Gradac River', 'Valjevo / Gradac River', '€10–€20', 'Car', 44.25, 19.8833, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-07', 'Niš Silver Filigree Master Workshops', 'Filigranske radionice srebra u Nišu', 'History', 'Witness master filigree artisans shape fine silver wire into delicate lace jewellery, preserving a Balkan metalworking craft originating in Byzantine times.', 'Svedočite veštini filigranista koji od tanke srebrne žice stvaraju delikatni nakit, čuvajući balkanski metalurški zanat vizantijskih korena.', 'Niš is one of Serbia''s historic sanctuaries for silver filigree craftsmanship. Working with fine gauge silver wire, master artisans twist, solder, and assemble delicate lacelike ornaments, earrings, and brooches using small handheld tweezers and soldering torches. Studio demonstrations showcase the meticulous patience, design mastery, and Balkan filigree heritage.', 'Niš predstavlja istorijski centar filigranskog zanata u Srbiji. Koristeći finu srebrnu žicu, majstori uvijaju, leme i spajaju mrežaste komade nakita i ukrasa pomoću pinceta i gorionika. Poseta radionici otkriva izuzetnu preciznost i tradiciju izrade srebrnog nakita.', '/src/assets/images/nis_fortress_stambol_gate_1778845134540.webp', '1.5–2 Hours', '2.5 Hours from Belgrade', 150, 'Niš', 'Niš', '€15–€35', 'Car', 43.3209, 21.8958, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-08', 'Srem Oak & Acacia Cooperage Workshops', 'Pinterske radionice hrastovih i bagremovih buradi u Sremu', 'Gastronomy', 'Step into traditional Srem cooperage workshops to see master pinteri shape seasoned oak and acacia staves over open fires to craft wine and rakija barrels.', 'Uđite u tradicionalne sremske pinterske radionice i posmatrajte oblikovanje hrastovih i bagremovih duga nad vatrom za izradu buradi za vino i rakiju.', 'Srem''s rich winemaking and rakija culture relies heavily on master coopers (pinteri). Selecting naturally seasoned local oak and acacia wood, craftsmen shape curved wooden staves, heat them over open fire hearths to bend the wood without splitting, and drive heavy iron hoops around the barrels. Visitors observe stave planing, fire toasting, and hoop fitting.', 'Vinarska i rakijska kultura Srema neodvojiva je od pinterskog zanata. Koristeći odležano hrastovo i bagremovo drvo, majstori savijaju dužice nad otvorenom vatrom i utežu ih gvozdenim obručima. Poseta radionici prikazuje obradu drveta, paljenje buradi i uvid u sazrevanje pića.', '/src/assets/images/sremski_karlovci_town_1778841131222.webp', '1.5–2.5 Hours', '1 Hour from Belgrade', 60, 'Sremska Mitrovica / Fruška Gora', 'Sremska Mitrovica / Fruška Gora', '€10–€25', 'Car', 44.9764, 19.6122, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-09', 'Svrljig Frula & Gajde Instrument Carving', 'Radionice izrade frula i gajdi u Svrljigu', 'History', 'Discover how traditional wooden flutes (frula) and Svrljig bagpipes (gajde) are hand-carved, tuned, and tested in South-Eastern Serbia.', 'Otkrijte kako se drvene frule i svrljiške gajde ručno dube, podešavaju i štimuju u tradicionalnim radionicama jugoistočne Srbije.', 'The Svrljig area is legendary for its folk music traditions and master wind instrument makers. Craftsmen select plum, maple, and boxwood timber, seasoning the wood before hand-boring, carving fingerholes, and tuning acoustic pitch. Visits include demonstrations of wooden frula carving, hornhead bagpipe assembly, and short traditional acoustic performances.', 'Svrljiški kraj je čuven po muzičkoj tradiciji i majstorima za izradu narodnih duvačkih instrumenata. Odabirom šljivovog i javorovog drveta, majstori ručno dube frule i izrađuju gajde sa autentičnim zvučnim štimom. Poseta uključuje prikaz izrade i kratku zvučnu demonstraciju.', '/src/assets/images/g-09_svrljig_frula_gajde_instrument_carving.webp', '1.5–2.5 Hours', '2.5 Hours from Belgrade', 160, 'Svrljig / Eastern Serbia', 'Svrljig / Eastern Serbia', '€10–€25', 'Car', 43.4136, 22.0864, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE),
  ('G-10', 'Pešter Plateau Artisan Dairy Households', 'Seoska domaćinstva za proizvodnju sira na Pešterskoj visoravni', 'Gastronomy', 'Visit traditional high-altitude mountain households on the Pešter Plateau to taste Sjenica white cheese aged in traditional wooden vats.', 'Obiđite visoko-planinska domaćinstva na Pešterskoj visoravni i probajte sjenički beli sir sazrevao u drvenim kacama.', 'High on the windswept Pešter Plateau, sheep and cattle graze vast alpine pastures producing milk for famed Sjenica cheese. Pastoral households maintain time-honored dairy practices, curdling fresh milk and aging brine-soaked cheeses in traditional wooden vats. Visitors experience mountain hospitality, view traditional dairy pantries, and sample artisanal cheeses.', 'Na prostranoj Pešterskoj visoravni, stada pasu na čestim planinskim pašnjacima dajući mleko vrhunskog kvaliteta za sjenički sir. Seoska domaćinstva čuvaju tradiciju prerade mleka i sazrevanja sira u drvenim kacama. Poseta nudi planinsko gostoprimstvo, obilazak mlekara i degustaciju sira.', '/src/assets/images/pirot_gastronomy_cheese_1778845871088.webp', '2–3 Hours', '4 Hours from Belgrade', 240, 'Sjenica / Pešter Plateau', 'Sjenica / Pešter Plateau', '€15–€35', 'Car', 43.2711, 20.0019, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, TRUE)
